ember/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T16:13:25-07:00","id":460464,"title":"","content":"I hope we get some more information on Mots. That was a part of Blasphemies that I was pretty interested in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T23:34:05-07:00","id":460761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/389486-dark-eras-viking-werewolves-need-your-help?p=460464#post460464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope we get some more information on Mots. That was a part of Blasphemies that I was pretty interested in.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are Mots, basically? And where in <b>Blasphemies</b> they are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T23:37:32-07:00","id":460764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/389486-dark-eras-viking-werewolves-need-your-help?p=460761#post460761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are Mots, basically? And where in <b>Blasphemies</b> they are?</div> </div> </div> </div>Moots, maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T23:41:53-07:00","id":460767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/389486-dark-eras-viking-werewolves-need-your-help?p=460761#post460761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are Mots, basically? And where in <b>Blasphemies</b> they are?</div> </div> </div> </div>Near the end of the chapter on Lodges, I think it was Chapter 3 or 4. They're basically a type of Lodge that all center around old Germanic and Norse myth/culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T23:43:45-07:00","id":460768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanandithras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/389486-dark-eras-viking-werewolves-need-your-help?p=460764#post460764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moots, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Page 97, in Chapter 3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mots are lodges linked by theme, culture and tradition. First and foremost, they combine a strong warrior ethic, with a passion for artistry and lore, including poetry, historical texts, linguistics and so on. Mots are also characterized in particular by an often dangerous practice of ritual oaths \u2014 special rites that cement ties between individuals and sometimes between mots or packs. These alliances shift from time to time, but are never taken lightly and are one reason for the mots\u2019 ability to persevere over time and for some of the bloody struggles that have plagued them. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T04:03:49-07:00","id":460915,"title":"","content":"I read more on Mots, and we totally need them in the Viking <b>Werewolf</b> chapter, at least story of creation of those!<br /> <br /> Basically, they are coalition (?) of Norse based Lodges, that have they own mythological bits and pieces added to general Uratha culture - and more bloody Gathras than other wolves. In reality, they are what would Norse Uratha society be like.<br /> <br /> They will totally go in to my second season of Sweden game, that I plan, hopefully, to mix with Viking Era, on the end of this year! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Other question come to mine mind them - what about <b>Apocalypse</b> like Get of Fenris? Could he work nicely with Mots of <b>Forsaken</b>, as interesting multi-Lodge North pattern?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-29-2015, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T06:11:35-07:00","id":460984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/389486-dark-eras-viking-werewolves-need-your-help?p=460915#post460915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read more on Mots, and we totally need them in the Viking <b>Werewolf</b> chapter, at least story of creation of those!<br /> <br /> Basically, they are coalition (?) of Norse based Lodges, that have they own mythological bits and pieces added to general Uratha culture - and more bloody Gathras than other wolves. In reality, they are what would Norse Uratha society be like.<br /> <br /> They will totally go in to my second season of Sweden game, that I plan, hopefully, to mix with Viking Era, on the end of this year! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Other question come to mine mind them - what about <b>Apocalypse</b> like Get of Fenris? Could he work nicely with Mots of <b>Forsaken</b>, as interesting multi-Lodge North pattern?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Get could totally work as a Mot, but I see them more as something that only accepts Blood Talons and certain Ghost Wolves because they consider themselves the children of Fenrir. That being said, there COULD be a Fenrir-Ur that is lesser in strength but similar to Fenris-Ur, who claims that Fenris is a fraud, and that the REAL Fenrir is bound beneath the Earth with chains of agonizing silver as a result of being usurped by one of his cubs. You could go a step further and say there are some remarkable similarities to Silver Wolf for this Fenrir-Ur, and the Get of Fenris were stereotypically portrayed, in certain editions of Forsaken, as having some eugenics-ish and racist tendencies....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T18:07:27-07:00","id":464107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/389486-dark-eras-viking-werewolves-need-your-help?p=460984#post460984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Get could totally work as a Mot, but I see them more as something that only accepts Blood Talons and certain Ghost Wolves because they consider themselves the children of Fenrir. That being said, there COULD be a Fenrir-Ur that is lesser in strength but similar to Fenris-Ur, who claims that Fenris is a fraud, and that the REAL Fenrir is bound beneath the Earth with chains of agonizing silver as a result of being usurped by one of his cubs. You could go a step further and say there are some remarkable similarities to Silver Wolf for this Fenrir-Ur, and the Get of Fenris were stereotypically portrayed, in certain editions of Forsaken, as having some eugenics-ish and racist tendencies....</div> </div> </div> </div>Is not the Eiwaz Mot the modern version of Get of Fenris? Really, they only need to re-name Noble Wolf for the Fenrir-Ur...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T18:09:52-07:00","id":464113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/389486-dark-eras-viking-werewolves-need-your-help?p=464107#post464107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is not the Eiwaz Mot the modern version of Get of Fenris? Really, they only need to re-name Noble Wolf for the Fenrir-Ur...</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T18:41:57-07:00","id":464130,"title":"","content":"How so? What are the key difference between <i>Get</i> and <i>Eiwaz</i>, beside the name of their patron?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T19:35:39-07:00","id":464190,"title":"","content":"*Sigh* Just... *sigh*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T19:52:28-07:00","id":464197,"title":"","content":"<b>Ephsy</b>, just spill it. I'm rather nWoDer, seen <b>Apocalypse</b> like a 15 years ago, have fascination of it about 3 months, read a novel anthology and moved on, because of crunch with things that <b>Forsaken</b> 2ed finally done good to werewolves mythos ( Eco-terrorists, I see you ).<br /> <br /> But I'm not limited and do really want to <i>understand</i> - especially, as I really pumped up for Norse themes in Werewolf game. I returned to <b>Forsaken</b> fold, because of this and plan Norse-inspired game. And maybe mixing the <i>Get of Fenris</i> &quot;true undestanding&quot; with <i>Eiwaz</i> openess on mythos would solve a big setting gap problems here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T20:04:13-07:00","id":464215,"title":"","content":"You're basically saying &quot;All of the Get of Fenris are racists/thugs/criminals/etc&quot; That's your argument to say Eiwaz Mot equals the Get of Fenris. A blanket statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}